WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.318
Secure IPC starts with a boundary mindset.

2
00:00:03.318 --> 00:00:11.376
Local communication can cross user, session, privilege, service, container, and lifecycle boundaries, so connection success should never

3
00:00:11.376 --> 00:00:13.272
automatically become operation authority.

4
00:00:13.272 --> 00:00:18.960
Choose IPC mechanisms that make identity, permissions, validation, and failure behavior reviewable.

5
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.330
Validate every message before trust.

6
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:27.492
Define message types, versions, required fields, sizes, ranges, state requirements, and unsupported behavior.

7
00:00:27.492 --> 00:00:35.076
Convert accepted messages into narrow internal types, and authorize each sensitive operation close to the boundary.

8
00:00:35.076 --> 00:00:36.498
Bound resources deliberately.

9
00:00:36.498 --> 00:00:45.030
Limit message size, queue growth, active requests, processing time, shared-memory mappings, handle transfer, and per-connection memory.

10
00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:50.718
Treat handles and descriptors as capabilities with ownership, cleanup, and permission rules.

11
00:00:50.718 --> 00:00:54.036
Finally, design for failure and test it.

12
00:00:54.036 --> 00:01:01.146
Cover malformed, unauthorized, oversized, incomplete, duplicate, out-of-order, timeout, cancellation, disconnect, and shutdown cases.

13
00:01:01.146 --> 00:01:03.990
Log safe categories without exposing secrets.

14
00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:12.522
Review IPC changes as security-critical because they connect local authority, parsing, concurrency, resources, and operating-system behavior.

15
00:01:12.522 --> 00:01:21.528
These habits keep local communication understandable as systems grow from one helper process into a larger multi-process architecture.

16
00:01:21.528 --> 00:01:30.534
They also make future platform changes, permission changes, and helper-process redesigns easier to assess before release, deployment, maintenance,

17
00:01:30.534 --> 00:01:34.800
support, audits, ownership transfer, and team handoffs later safely.
